{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 867 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "2fa1c6902af02ed69056f810712d6d13577246144a21c121d561dadaf45c661c" :edb/db-before-t 866 :edb/db-after-t 867 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534179 50 #inst "2026-10-11T17:28:39.024Z" 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186088155 1068 #edb/ref 17592186085584 13194139534179 17592186045417 false] [17592186088155 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413286 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186088155 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186088155 1071 "A  linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation. Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}48 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$" 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186088155 1071 "A linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation. Given that $v = \\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $T(v) = \\begin{bmatrix}48 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}$, what is the standard matrix of $T$?" 13194139534179 17592186045417 false] [17592186088155 1074 "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}48 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =6\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =6v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=6v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=6.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186100931 1038 #edb/ref 17592186413290 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186184190 1038 #edb/ref 17592186413289 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413274 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413291 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413274 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413292 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413274 1043 #edb/ref 1759218