[17592186413289 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413289 1071 "The fifth-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=1$ is given by\n\n$$\n{P}_{5}(x)=6+12(x-1)+9(x-1)^{2}+4(x-1)^{3}+\\frac{5}{4}(x-1)^{4}+\\frac{3}{10}(x-1)^{5}.\n$$\n\nWhat is ${f}^{(5)}(1)?$\n\n${f}^{(5)}(1)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413289 1072 #uuid "23470b63-10f9-5736-89ca-b9c89f21d360" 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413289 1074 "The coefficient of $(x-1)^{5}$ is given by $\\frac{{f}^{(5)}(1)}{5!}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{f}^{(5)}(1)}{5!} & =\\frac{3}{10} \\\\ \\frac{{f}^{(5)}(1)}{120} & =\\frac{3}{10} \\\\ {f}^{(5)}(1) & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413290 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413288 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413290 1069 "q-81675" 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413290 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413290 1071 "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ about $x=0$ is" 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413290 1072 #uuid "ca3460ff-fc6a-5037-a239-c26e4d66f531" 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413290 1074 "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!} \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) & ⟹ &  & f(0) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡0=0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=2 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡0=0 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(0) & =-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =0+2\\cdot x+0\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+(-8)\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{6} \\\\  & =2x-\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413291 1062 #uuid "27bb1f1e-f0b6-55ad-af80-59be0e465969" 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413291 1063 #edb/ref 17592186413290 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413292 1058 #edb/ref 17592186413295 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413292 1062 #uuid "506e12af-bf04-5946-bba6-af1152b8d511" 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413292 1063 #edb/ref 17592186284720 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413293 1058 #edb/ref 17592186413294 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413293 1062 #uuid "554297ff-234a-52b4-a1a0-951148703885" 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413293 1063 #edb/ref 17592186351248 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413294 1058 #edb/ref 17592186413291 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413294 1062 #uuid "6697871d-2836-5bef-816e-0b7ddadc99a2" 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413294 1063 #edb/ref 17592186088028 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413295 1058 #edb/ref 17592186413299 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413295 1062 #uuid "9df23eb1-7334-5ee3-99e0-0928ef712e13" 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413295 1063 #edb/ref 17592186088155 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413296 1058 #edb/ref 17592186413293 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413296 1062 #uuid "a93ae252-6828-598e-a0ad-d2413fcaf43a" 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413296 1063 #edb/ref 17592186290295 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [17592186413297 1058 #edb/ref 17592186413292 13194139534179 17592186045417 true] [175921864